Error: Jet.FloatInfinitySeedIntOnly: `best` is a Float seeded with -infinity, but every value assigned to it is an Int
  --> Tests/UI/float_infinity_seed_int_only.jet:5:12
    |
  5 |     best := -math.INFINITY
    |     ^^^^
 Why: Each Int widens to Float as it is assigned, so the result reads `5.0` where the input held `5`, and an Int beyond 2^53 stops the program
 Fix: Make `best` an `Int?` that starts as `None`, or an Int that starts at `Int.MIN`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FloatInfinitySeedIntOnly

Error: Jet.FloatInfinitySeedIntOnly: `least` is a Float seeded with infinity, but every value assigned to it is an Int
  --> Tests/UI/float_infinity_seed_int_only.jet:13:13
    |
 13 |     least := Float.INFINITY
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: Each Int widens to Float as it is assigned, so the result reads `5.0` where the input held `5`, and an Int beyond 2^53 stops the program
 Fix: Make `least` an `Int?` that starts as `None`, or an Int that starts at `Int.MAX`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FloatInfinitySeedIntOnly
